Spoiler (major one)

Polypiling is, depending on who you ask, a powerful way to get what you
want in the game that is either outright cheating or fair.  I think most
people will agree that it's an "abuse" though.

What you do is this:

Get yourself a wand of polymorph.  The spell may work too.  Then, find
a level with lots of junk on it.  A shop level works nicely.

Gather all of the junk you can find into one pile, including rocks,
all weapons, including daggers, arrows, etc.  Dead bodies work too.

Then, zap the pile with your trusty wand of polymorph.

You have a pile of new stuff!  Sort through the pile, take what you want,
and zap again.  Repeat until you run out of charges.  It's fun!

Actually, most people consider this an unfair practice because it's too
easy to get all kinds of cool stuff.  The Gods of Nethack have changed
the rules over time to make Polypiling less profitable, ie, you can't
generate Artifacts (Excaliber, Stormbringer, etc.), wands of wishing,
magic lamps, or the Amulet of Yendor.  You can make just about anything
else though.

Personally, I condider it fair if you don't abuse it.  It is allowed in
the scope of the game.  The programmers know it exists and have not
removed it.  Guess it's up to you.  If I happen to find a wand of poly-
morphing and have a nice pile of junk, like from a soldier room, I will
go ahead and zap the pile a few times.  I DON'T purposely go around
with this as a goal in mind though.

A few points.  You can only polymorph an item to the same type of item.
For instance, wands will only become other wands and armor will only
become other armor.  Also, the cursed/blessed +/- status will remain
the same as the original item you zapped.  

Also, I believe that if you zap an artifact it will become a plain
weapon.  I've never done this though, as the point of the trick is to
create good stuff from useless junk....

